		(descr "Pololu #2813 Big Pushbutton Power Switch with Reverse Voltage Protection HP soldered flush on its land, top view of the module as it sits on the board (dimension drawing psw03b, 12 January 2016): 16 holes D1.02 in two columns 17.78 apart, 1.27 mm from the side edges, pitch 2.54, lowest 2.54 from the bottom edge (VIN column VIN, VIN, GND, GND, ON, OFF, CTRL, GND and VOUT column VOUT, VOUT, GND, GND, B, A, A, GND from the large-hole end, bottom-view callouts mirrored); 4 large holes D2.18 (VIN, GND, GND, VOUT) at pitch 5.00, 2.29 from the top edge and 2.66 from the side edges, here plated 2.2 mm holes for 18 AWG links (Pololu: above 5 A use the large holes or both 0.1 in holes per node); board 20.32 x 25.4, parts 2.4 above its 1.57 mm board")
